1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,000
INTERNET CAFE

2
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:02,000
[Leorio] No good.

3
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:03,000
I've got nothing.

4
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:08,000
That two billion per Spider reward
is pretty attractive, but…

5
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:11,000
finding them will be impossible.

6
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:12,000
[Gon] Yeah…

7
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:14,000
Hey!

8
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:17,000
We could ask for concrete information
on the website.

9
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:18,000
Maybe we could even ask

10
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:20,000
about the Phantom Troupe’s
current location.

11
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:23,000
It might help,
if we offered a really big reward.

12
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:25,000
We could, but...

13
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:27,000
we don’t have nearly
enough money for that.

14
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:29,000
[Gon] Not a problem.

15
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:32,000
HUNTER LICENSE

16
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:40,000
[theme song playing]

17
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:56,000
VERY x SHARP x EYE

18
00:01:57,000 --> 00:01:59,000
[narrator] Gon and his friends
are in pursuit

19
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:01,000
of the elusive Phantom Troupe

20
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:05,000
and have now obtained the funds
to buy the information they need.

21
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:09,000
[Leorio] That’s crazy!

22
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:11,000
You actually have the money!

23
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:15,000
Idiot. I can’t believe you actually pawned
your Hunter’s License.

24
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:16,000
You’re insane, you know that?

25
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:19,000
So, what do you think we should do first?

26
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:23,000
To start with we should buy ourselves
a Southernbees catalog.

27
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:31,000
Here is this year’s official
Southernbees auction catalog, gentlemen.

28
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:33,000
[Gon] Thank you!

29
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:41,000
Got it! Greed Island’s right here!

30
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:44,000
[Leorio] Seven total units on sale…

31
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:46,000
Wow. Minimum starting bid is...

32
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:48,000
8.9 billion.

33
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:51,000
No change there.

34
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:57,000
Now we just have to wait
for the information to start rollin’ in.

35
00:02:57,000 --> 00:03:00,000
So first, we’ll catch one of the Spiders

36
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:01,000
and after that,

37
00:03:01,000 --> 00:03:02,000
all we have to do

38
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:05,000
is make ‘em tell us
where the rest of ‘em are hiding. Easy!

39
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:06,000
What the--?

40
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:08,000
What’s wrong? Gon?

41
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:11,000
This thing is…

42
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:14,000
Look at that!
You found a Ben’s knife, huh?

43
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:15,000
Wait, what’s a Ben’s knife?

44
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:19,000
It’s a knife that a mass murderer
designed about a hundred years ago.

45
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:22,000
The guy was also a famous blacksmith.

46
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:24,000
This looks like one of his original works.

47
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:28,000
It’s a lesser known piece
a lot of rabid collectors are after.

48
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:30,000
Good eye, Gon!

49
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:32,000
I didn’t have any idea what it was.

50
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:33,000
[Killua and Leorio] Huh?

51
00:03:33,000 --> 00:03:35,000
It just caught my attention is all.

52
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:37,000
I guess I got curious,

53
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:39,000
so I used Gyo on it.

54
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:41,000
And that’s when I noticed a faint aura.

55
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:42,000
What’s Gyo?

56
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:44,000
Gyo’s a form of Nen.

57
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:48,000
It’s basically when you look really,
really closely at something.

58
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:50,000
[Leorio - focusing grunt]

59
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:51,000
Wow, you weren’t kidding!

60
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:53,000
Here, let me see that.

61
00:03:54,000 --> 00:03:55,000
[focusing grunt]

62
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:58,000
[Leorio] Nope. I don’t see a thing.

63
00:03:58,000 --> 00:04:00,000
You will once you get
more training in Ren.

64
00:04:01,000 --> 00:04:03,000
Oh, yeah! There’s another way to do it!

65
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:04,000
Do what?

66
00:04:04,000 --> 00:04:05,000
Another way we can make money.

67
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:08,000
Don’t you remember
what Four Eyes said to us?

68
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:10,000
When we were at Heavens Arena?

69
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:15,000
He said some really talented people
can use Nen without even knowing!

70
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:17,000
Who the hell is Four Eyes?

71
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:19,000
[Killua] Wing.

72
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:21,000
He’s the one who taught us Nen.

73
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:23,000
So, this knife had aura.

74
00:04:23,000 --> 00:04:26,000
I say we search
for other things that do, too.

75
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:29,000
Find one and it’s a good bet
that it was made by a real master!

76
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:31,000
I get it!

77
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:32,000
So, we can find hidden gems

78
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:35,000
but without having
to go through a bunch of training

79
00:04:35,000 --> 00:04:36,000
to be professional appraisers!

80
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:40,000
And then we just auction off
what we find at a higher price!

81
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:41,000
If you want it,

82
00:04:41,000 --> 00:04:44,000
all you gotta do is write your price down.

83
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:48,000
You mean, customers get to name
their own prices?

84
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:51,000
[hawker] Yeah.
That’s the way this market works.

85
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:53,000
You write down whatever it is
you’re willing to pay,

86
00:04:53,000 --> 00:04:55,000
and when the time expires,

87
00:04:56,000 --> 00:04:59,000
the item goes to whoever
had the highest bid.

88
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:02,000
See, this here is a really popular item.

89
00:05:03,000 --> 00:05:06,000
Just look how the price
shot up near the end.

90
00:05:07,000 --> 00:05:09,000
I get it now.

91
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:15,000
Well? Let’s get started!

92
00:05:16,000 --> 00:05:18,000
Sounds good.
I’ll check out the online forums.

93
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:19,000
[Gon] Hm.

94
00:05:22,000 --> 00:05:24,000
[Gon] Hmm...

95
00:05:25,000 --> 00:05:27,000
This vase is pretty weird

96
00:05:27,000 --> 00:05:29,000
but I’m picking up aura from it.

97
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:32,000
There’s a bid!

98
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:34,000
If there’s already a bid,

99
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:37,000
then you should enter one
that’s two and a half times higher.

100
00:05:38,000 --> 00:05:39,000
You might end up bidding too high

101
00:05:39,000 --> 00:05:42,000
but at least that way
you’ll scare off any rivals.

102
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:46,000
[Gon] Five hundred times two and a half…

103
00:05:46,000 --> 00:05:48,000
Let me see...

104
00:05:49,000 --> 00:05:50,000
Uh!

105
00:05:56,000 --> 00:05:57,000
It’s the same person!

106
00:05:59,000 --> 00:06:00,000
Same there?

107
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:02,000
Yeah, I found a couple of items

108
00:06:02,000 --> 00:06:05,000
but both of them had bids
placed by “Zepile” already.

109
00:06:06,000 --> 00:06:08,000
I bid two and a half times higher

110
00:06:08,000 --> 00:06:11,000
but as soon as I did, he quadrupled it.

111
00:06:11,000 --> 00:06:13,000
Then it’s not a coincidence.

112
00:06:13,000 --> 00:06:14,000
No.

113
00:06:14,000 --> 00:06:15,000
[Gon] What now?

114
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:17,000
We need to keep placing bids,

115
00:06:17,000 --> 00:06:19,000
all the way up to the deadline.

116
00:06:19,000 --> 00:06:20,000
There are two of us,

117
00:06:21,000 --> 00:06:23,000
so I’m sure we’re bound to win something.

118
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:24,000
Yeah, okay.

119
00:06:29,000 --> 00:06:31,000
In the end we won three and lost one.

120
00:06:32,000 --> 00:06:34,000
Yeah. They got that weird vase
at the last minute.

121
00:06:35,000 --> 00:06:37,000
{Killua] Not too bad,
all things considered.

122
00:06:37,000 --> 00:06:40,000
Come on, let’s take ‘em
to the auction house now.

123
00:06:43,000 --> 00:06:45,000
Oh, I’m terribly sorry…

124
00:06:45,000 --> 00:06:48,000
but the auction house
simply can’t accept any additional items

125
00:06:48,000 --> 00:06:50,000
once the catalog has been published.

126
00:06:50,000 --> 00:06:52,000
You’re too late, I’m afraid.

127
00:06:52,000 --> 00:06:53,000
Uh...

128
00:06:53,000 --> 00:06:54,000
Can you make an exception?

129
00:06:55,000 --> 00:06:57,000
See, we really had our hearts
set on auctioning off these items!

130
00:06:58,000 --> 00:06:59,000
Hmm...

131
00:06:59,000 --> 00:07:01,000
Perhaps you might be interested

132
00:07:02,000 --> 00:07:03,000
in trying your luck over
at the dealer’s market.

133
00:07:04,000 --> 00:07:05,000
[both] The Dealer’s market?

134
00:07:08,000 --> 00:07:09,000
[Gon] So this is it.

135
00:07:09,000 --> 00:07:11,000
The pros will be here,

136
00:07:11,000 --> 00:07:14,000
so if any of these are genuine
we should get a great price.

137
00:07:14,000 --> 00:07:17,000
Yeah, I know, but I really wanted
to sell these at the auction.

138
00:07:17,000 --> 00:07:19,000
How much do you think we’re gonna get?

139
00:07:19,000 --> 00:07:21,000
There’s only one way to find out!

140
00:07:25,000 --> 00:07:28,000
Oh… You say you found these
in your storehouse?

141
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:30,000
Yeah! And my dad said
that we should sell ‘em

142
00:07:30,000 --> 00:07:32,000
if the price was good enough.

143
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:35,000
These are excellent pieces.

144
00:07:35,000 --> 00:07:37,000
Only fifty copies were printed,

145
00:07:37,000 --> 00:07:40,000
and yours has a single-digit
serial number,

146
00:07:40,000 --> 00:07:42,000
not to mention an authentic autograph.

147
00:07:43,000 --> 00:07:44,000
{Killua] Yeah, we know.

148
00:07:44,000 --> 00:07:46,000
[Gon] That’s where the aura
was coming from.

149
00:07:47,000 --> 00:07:49,000
[shop owner]
It’s worth at least 150,000.

150
00:07:51,000 --> 00:07:54,000
And look at this antique doll!

151
00:07:54,000 --> 00:07:56,000
It’s in great shape.

152
00:07:56,000 --> 00:07:59,000
Both the doll and box are pristine,
which raises the value.

153
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:02,000
Three hundred thousand I’d guess.

154
00:08:02,000 --> 00:08:03,000
But…

155
00:08:04,000 --> 00:08:07,000
I’m sorry to say this one
isn’t worth nearly as much.

156
00:08:08,000 --> 00:08:09,000
[both] Oh...

157
00:08:09,000 --> 00:08:11,000
[shop owner] The box and statue
are from different periods.

158
00:08:12,000 --> 00:08:14,000
The box was made recently.

159
00:08:14,000 --> 00:08:18,000
The statue is roughly carved
and doesn’t adhere to any theme.

160
00:08:18,000 --> 00:08:21,000
I’d say it’s only worth 1,500 Jenny.

161
00:08:22,000 --> 00:08:25,000
[Gon] But there’s a little aura
coming from it…

162
00:08:25,000 --> 00:08:28,000
Now don’t worry.
That’s just the price as an artwork.

163
00:08:28,000 --> 00:08:32,000
But the wood it’s made of
is actually quite valuable.

164
00:08:32,000 --> 00:08:33,000
[Gon and Killua] Huh?

165
00:08:33,000 --> 00:08:36,000
I would be more than happy
to make you an offer on it.

166
00:08:37,000 --> 00:08:39,000
Sell me the painting and doll
for 420,000

167
00:08:40,000 --> 00:08:42,000
and I’ll throw in another 80,000
for the wood.

168
00:08:43,000 --> 00:08:44,000
So, 500,000 total?

169
00:08:45,000 --> 00:08:46,000
What do you think?

170
00:08:46,000 --> 00:08:48,000
There’s no rush.
Take your time.

171
00:08:49,000 --> 00:08:51,000
But I doubt you’re going
to find a better offer

172
00:08:51,000 --> 00:08:52,000
from anyone else around here.

173
00:08:53,000 --> 00:08:54,000
In the meantime,

174
00:08:54,000 --> 00:08:57,000
let me analyze this and find out
the exact age of the wood.

175
00:08:58,000 --> 00:08:59,000
[man 1] Stop right there!

176
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:02,000
Put that statue down, now.

177
00:09:03,000 --> 00:09:04,000
I’m sorry, but who are you?

178
00:09:05,000 --> 00:09:07,000
Watch out. This guy is a scammer.

179
00:09:08,000 --> 00:09:10,000
That’s a fair price
for the doll and painting

180
00:09:10,000 --> 00:09:12,000
but he’s lying to your face
about the statue!

181
00:09:12,000 --> 00:09:15,000
I-- I’m not lying; I swear I’m not!

182
00:09:15,000 --> 00:09:17,000
You sure about that?

183
00:09:17,000 --> 00:09:20,000
Because no collector
would pay 80,000 for that wood!

184
00:09:20,000 --> 00:09:22,000
All you’re interested in

185
00:09:23,000 --> 00:09:24,000
is the contents of that statue!

186
00:09:34,000 --> 00:09:36,000
That’s actually a wooden vault.

187
00:09:36,000 --> 00:09:37,000
[Gon and Killua]
Wait, are you serious?

188
00:09:37,000 --> 00:09:39,000
Three hundred years ago,

189
00:09:39,000 --> 00:09:43,000
secret vaults like this were a popular way
for the wealthy to evade taxes.

190
00:09:43,000 --> 00:09:44,000
[Gon] I didn’t know that.

191
00:09:45,000 --> 00:09:47,000
[man] If it’s the real deal,

192
00:09:47,000 --> 00:09:50,000
then there should be
some sort of valuable stuffed inside.

193
00:09:50,000 --> 00:09:52,000
You planned on stealing its contents

194
00:09:52,000 --> 00:09:55,000
while you were just pretending
to analyze its age!

195
00:09:55,000 --> 00:09:57,000
No! No, I would never do that!

196
00:09:57,000 --> 00:09:58,000
[man 2] Hold on!

197
00:09:59,000 --> 00:10:03,000
Do you have any proof at all
that that thing’s a genuine wooden vault?

198
00:10:03,000 --> 00:10:04,000
[man 1] What was that?

199
00:10:05,000 --> 00:10:08,000
It’s fairly obvious that the wood
is over 300 years old.

200
00:10:09,000 --> 00:10:12,000
But all that tells us
is the age of the raw material.

201
00:10:13,000 --> 00:10:14,000
It could have been carved recently.

202
00:10:16,000 --> 00:10:19,000
That’s a doctoring method
called a “facelift”, boys.

203
00:10:19,000 --> 00:10:20,000
A doctoring method?

204
00:10:21,000 --> 00:10:25,000
He means when a counterfeiter
tries to trick a professional appraiser.

205
00:10:25,000 --> 00:10:26,000
But that isn’t what I’m doing.

206
00:10:27,000 --> 00:10:30,000
An amateur would never recognize
this seam here.

207
00:10:31,000 --> 00:10:33,000
A seam which contains a type of glue

208
00:10:33,000 --> 00:10:36,000
that was commonly used
in that time period.

209
00:10:36,000 --> 00:10:39,000
You’re insisting this
is a real wooden vault, are you?

210
00:10:39,000 --> 00:10:40,000
[man 1] Yeah.

211
00:10:42,000 --> 00:10:44,000
But it’s possible that it’s been opened,

212
00:10:44,000 --> 00:10:47,000
the contents swapped out
and then the statue was reassembled…

213
00:10:48,000 --> 00:10:50,000
something we call a “transplant”.

214
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:53,000
When a counterfeiter
performs a transplant,

215
00:10:53,000 --> 00:10:56,000
they put a new coat of glue
on top of the old one,

216
00:10:56,000 --> 00:10:58,000
creating a secondary seal.

217
00:10:58,000 --> 00:11:01,000
But only a rank amateur
would even think of trying that.

218
00:11:03,000 --> 00:11:06,000
A pro would melt the glue with a flame,
then reseal it.

219
00:11:07,000 --> 00:11:10,000
That would make it look like
the statue had never been opened.

220
00:11:10,000 --> 00:11:12,000
It’s known as “cauterization”.

221
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:15,000
[man 1] It’s not cauterized!

222
00:11:16,000 --> 00:11:18,000
If someone had used a flame,
the wood would be scorched,

223
00:11:18,000 --> 00:11:21,000
or at the very least
the glue would be discolored.

224
00:11:21,000 --> 00:11:24,000
Even pros would have a hard time
spotting those details.

225
00:11:25,000 --> 00:11:26,000
Doesn’t prove anything.

226
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:29,000
I am a pro appraiser!

227
00:11:29,000 --> 00:11:30,000
I swear by my eyes

228
00:11:31,000 --> 00:11:33,000
this is a real wooden vault!

229
00:11:34,000 --> 00:11:35,000
It has never been opened

230
00:11:35,000 --> 00:11:38,000
and the treasure that’s inside
has never been swapped out!

231
00:11:40,000 --> 00:11:41,000
Okay.

232
00:11:42,000 --> 00:11:43,000
Just for the sake of argument,

233
00:11:43,000 --> 00:11:45,000
let’s say it is a genuine wooden vault.

234
00:11:46,000 --> 00:11:48,000
If the contents have been swapped out,

235
00:11:48,000 --> 00:11:50,000
what’ll you do?

236
00:11:50,000 --> 00:11:52,000
What are you willing to bet?

237
00:11:58,000 --> 00:12:00,000
If you’re right, I’ll be your lackey
for the rest of my life.

238
00:12:03,000 --> 00:12:04,000
[smirks]

239
00:12:05,000 --> 00:12:06,000
Give it up.

240
00:12:13,000 --> 00:12:14,000
[smirks]

241
00:12:15,000 --> 00:12:16,000
[both] Oh!

242
00:12:20,000 --> 00:12:23,000
[Gon and Killua] Whoa! Awesome!

243
00:12:26,000 --> 00:12:28,000
[Killua] Oh… So, you’re Zepile.

244
00:12:29,000 --> 00:12:30,000
Thanks a lot, Mister Zepile!

245
00:12:30,000 --> 00:12:32,000
Oh, there’s no need to thank me.

246
00:12:32,000 --> 00:12:34,000
It’s just a matter of give and take.

247
00:12:35,000 --> 00:12:36,000
Say twenty per cent?

248
00:12:36,000 --> 00:12:37,000
[both] Huh?

249
00:12:37,000 --> 00:12:39,000
[Zepile] My cut of the profit
when you sell the treasure.

250
00:12:39,000 --> 00:12:42,000
What?! Are you trying to rip us off,
old man?

251
00:12:42,000 --> 00:12:44,000
Now that was uncalled for.

252
00:12:44,000 --> 00:12:47,000
Look I’ve got to charge something
for advising you.

253
00:12:47,000 --> 00:12:48,000
It’s okay.

254
00:12:48,000 --> 00:12:50,000
He did help us out back there, after all.

255
00:12:51,000 --> 00:12:52,000
Gimme a break, man!

256
00:12:53,000 --> 00:12:56,000
We need to collect
as much Jenny as possible, remember?

257
00:12:57,000 --> 00:12:58,000
We can maybe buy him lunch.

258
00:12:58,000 --> 00:13:00,000
[Zepile] Oh, yeah?

259
00:13:00,000 --> 00:13:01,000
Sure, works for me.

260
00:13:02,000 --> 00:13:03,000
[both] Huh?

261
00:13:07,000 --> 00:13:09,000
[Gon] So, Mister Zepile…

262
00:13:09,000 --> 00:13:10,000
Hm?

263
00:13:10,000 --> 00:13:12,000
I feel kinda bad,
so we will pay you a commission.

264
00:13:12,000 --> 00:13:14,000
Dude! You’re such a pushover!

265
00:13:14,000 --> 00:13:17,000
Nah. Really, it’s perfectly okay.

266
00:13:17,000 --> 00:13:19,000
Just tell me one thing and we’ll be even.

267
00:13:19,000 --> 00:13:21,000
What was it that made you guys
bid on all these items?

268
00:13:21,000 --> 00:13:22,000
Something tipped you off.

269
00:13:24,000 --> 00:13:26,000
Well? Should we tell him the truth?

270
00:13:26,000 --> 00:13:29,000
Sure. It beats paying him, anyway.

271
00:13:30,000 --> 00:13:32,000
[Zepile] Ah. Nen Aura, huh?

272
00:13:33,000 --> 00:13:35,000
Well, if you’re being honest,

273
00:13:35,000 --> 00:13:37,000
that does explain
why you purchased that statue.

274
00:13:38,000 --> 00:13:41,000
It was pretty obvious you had no idea
something was hidden inside.

275
00:13:42,000 --> 00:13:45,000
So why do you two need money so badly?

276
00:13:46,000 --> 00:13:48,000
[Killua] We can tell you,
but not for free.

277
00:13:48,000 --> 00:13:50,000
You’ve got to answer
one of our questions, too.

278
00:13:51,000 --> 00:13:52,000
Great. You start.

279
00:13:53,000 --> 00:13:54,000
At the auction

280
00:13:55,000 --> 00:13:56,000
there’s an item we want to buy.

281
00:13:57,000 --> 00:13:58,000
So, we need money.

282
00:13:58,000 --> 00:14:00,000
Oh. Which item is it?

283
00:14:01,000 --> 00:14:02,000
[Killua] It’s our turn now.

284
00:14:03,000 --> 00:14:04,000
Three hundred million Jenny.

285
00:14:04,000 --> 00:14:07,000
That’s how much
you estimated this treasure’s worth.

286
00:14:07,000 --> 00:14:08,000
So, do you think

287
00:14:08,000 --> 00:14:11,000
that’s how much we could get
for it at the dealer’s market?

288
00:14:11,000 --> 00:14:12,000
At the dealer’s market?

289
00:14:13,000 --> 00:14:16,000
I don’t really know;
they deal mainly in hard cash.

290
00:14:16,000 --> 00:14:18,000
So, if you show up early on,

291
00:14:18,000 --> 00:14:20,000
it’s unlikely that you’ll get
a fair price for it.

292
00:14:20,000 --> 00:14:22,000
-What?!
-Seriously?

293
00:14:23,000 --> 00:14:24,000
[Zepile] Now it’s my turn.

294
00:14:24,000 --> 00:14:25,000
I'll repeat the question.

295
00:14:26,000 --> 00:14:28,000
Which item are you looking to bid on?

296
00:14:28,000 --> 00:14:31,000
It’s a video game called Greed Island.

297
00:14:31,000 --> 00:14:34,000
Ah! You mean the one
that’s super expensive?

298
00:14:34,000 --> 00:14:36,000
I’m real curious
about that weird vase you bought.

299
00:14:36,000 --> 00:14:38,000
How much do you think that it’s worth?

300
00:14:39,000 --> 00:14:40,000
What? This thing?

301
00:14:41,000 --> 00:14:43,000
It’s just a piece of junk.

302
00:14:43,000 --> 00:14:44,000
Totally worthless.

303
00:14:46,000 --> 00:14:48,000
I don’t get why you’d want
such an expensive game.

304
00:14:48,000 --> 00:14:51,000
Doesn’t it cost like six billion Jenny?

305
00:14:51,000 --> 00:14:52,000
[Killua] Starts at eight point nine.

306
00:14:53,000 --> 00:14:55,000
Thing is we’re trying
to find Gon’s father.

307
00:14:56,000 --> 00:14:58,000
We need to buy the game
because it has a clue inside.

308
00:14:59,000 --> 00:15:00,000
Oh…

309
00:15:00,000 --> 00:15:02,000
[Killua] So why did you pick that vase?

310
00:15:03,000 --> 00:15:06,000
Well, you knew that wooden vault
was the real thing, didn’t you?

311
00:15:06,000 --> 00:15:08,000
So, you could’ve bid on that.
But you didn’t.

312
00:15:08,000 --> 00:15:10,000
You bid on that weird vase instead.

313
00:15:11,000 --> 00:15:12,000
Why?

314
00:15:14,000 --> 00:15:15,000
Well, you see…

315
00:15:16,000 --> 00:15:18,000
I sort of made this vase myself.

316
00:15:18,000 --> 00:15:19,000
[both] Huh?

317
00:15:20,000 --> 00:15:22,000
“Sort of” because it isn’t
my original work.

318
00:15:22,000 --> 00:15:23,000
[Gon and Killua] Huh?

319
00:15:23,000 --> 00:15:24,000
This is a knock-off.

320
00:15:25,000 --> 00:15:26,000
In other words, it’s counterfeit.

321
00:15:27,000 --> 00:15:28,000
When I was poor,

322
00:15:28,000 --> 00:15:31,000
this was how I made my Jenny. Until…

323
00:15:31,000 --> 00:15:34,000
I became an appraiser
and started earning money.

324
00:15:34,000 --> 00:15:37,000
As soon as that happened,
I quit all of that.

325
00:15:38,000 --> 00:15:40,000
But when I see
how poorly made these things are...

326
00:15:40,000 --> 00:15:42,000
Oh boy, it’s really embarrassing.

327
00:15:44,000 --> 00:15:46,000
I swore I’d buy them back

328
00:15:46,000 --> 00:15:48,000
whenever I saw them at the market.

329
00:15:49,000 --> 00:15:51,000
Any clue what a real one would cost?

330
00:15:51,000 --> 00:15:52,000
[Zepile] My turn.

331
00:15:53,000 --> 00:15:55,000
What does your dad do for a living?

332
00:15:55,000 --> 00:15:57,000
He’s... a professional Hunter.

333
00:15:57,000 --> 00:16:00,000
I asked how much a real one would cost!

334
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:02,000
-Forty, fifty K.
-[Killua grumbles]

335
00:16:02,000 --> 00:16:05,000
Is that so? A pro Hunter, huh?

336
00:16:06,000 --> 00:16:08,000
There are a couple of them
in the antiques community

337
00:16:08,000 --> 00:16:11,000
and not one of 'em
is someone you would describe as ‘normal’.

338
00:16:12,000 --> 00:16:15,000
Won’t it be impossible
for you to find him on your own?

339
00:16:15,000 --> 00:16:16,000
We’ll be fine.

340
00:16:17,000 --> 00:16:18,000
See, I’m a pro Hunter myself.

341
00:16:19,000 --> 00:16:20,000
Wait-- really?!

342
00:16:21,000 --> 00:16:24,000
‘Kay. It’s your turn
to ask us a question now.

343
00:16:24,000 --> 00:16:25,000
Hmm...

344
00:16:26,000 --> 00:16:28,000
Right. This one’ll be my final question.

345
00:16:29,000 --> 00:16:32,000
Is there anything at all
I can help you with?

346
00:16:32,000 --> 00:16:33,000
[both] Huh?

347
00:16:34,000 --> 00:16:36,000
[Zepile] If you want to make money
at an auction,

348
00:16:36,000 --> 00:16:38,000
you’ll need someone
with appraisal experience.

349
00:16:38,000 --> 00:16:41,000
You could say that teaming up
with the right appraiser

350
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:44,000
can guarantee you a profit every time.

351
00:16:44,000 --> 00:16:48,000
You choose how much you want to pay me.
Whatever you think’s fair.

352
00:16:48,000 --> 00:16:49,000
How’s that?

353
00:16:50,000 --> 00:16:53,000
Fine. Then you have to answer
our last question.

354
00:16:53,000 --> 00:16:55,000
What made you want to help us out?

355
00:16:55,000 --> 00:16:56,000
What’s in it for you?

356
00:17:00,000 --> 00:17:01,000
[wry chuckle]

357
00:17:02,000 --> 00:17:04,000
-It just made me happy.
-[Gon and Killua] Huh?

358
00:17:04,000 --> 00:17:07,000
Felt nice that someone
was bidding on my work,

359
00:17:07,000 --> 00:17:09,000
even if it is just
a worthless piece of junk.

360
00:17:09,000 --> 00:17:11,000
It is not a piece of junk!

361
00:17:12,000 --> 00:17:13,000
That vase you made,

362
00:17:13,000 --> 00:17:16,000
it’s overflowing with your Nen,
Mister Zepile!

363
00:17:16,000 --> 00:17:19,000
Aura’s common and anybody can produce it

364
00:17:19,000 --> 00:17:23,000
but it’s incredibly difficult to control.
Like, really hard!

365
00:17:23,000 --> 00:17:27,000
You have to concentrate
and train for a really long time.

366
00:17:27,000 --> 00:17:30,000
Anybody can see how much effort
you put into making that vase.

367
00:17:30,000 --> 00:17:32,000
I know I sure can!

368
00:17:32,000 --> 00:17:34,000
This kind of work takes talent!

369
00:17:35,000 --> 00:17:38,000
And I’m sorry
for saying it was weird earlier.

370
00:17:41,000 --> 00:17:42,000
[sighs]

371
00:17:42,000 --> 00:17:44,000
I can trust my eyes;
they’ve never fooled me.

372
00:17:46,000 --> 00:17:48,000
When you appraise things long enough,

373
00:17:48,000 --> 00:17:50,000
you can’t help but become
a good judge of character.

374
00:17:51,000 --> 00:17:54,000
I look at the sellers and the buyers,

375
00:17:54,000 --> 00:17:55,000
not just the goods.

376
00:17:56,000 --> 00:17:59,000
If there’s one thing I’ve learned
after all this time appraising antiques,

377
00:18:00,000 --> 00:18:02,000
it’s that it’s a lot harder
to appraise people.

378
00:18:03,000 --> 00:18:04,000
And when I saw you,

379
00:18:05,000 --> 00:18:07,000
the appraiser in me knew right away…

380
00:18:08,000 --> 00:18:10,000
that I really wanted
to work with you. Truly.

381
00:18:11,000 --> 00:18:13,000
So that’s my answer.

382
00:18:13,000 --> 00:18:14,000
What's yours?

383
00:18:17,000 --> 00:18:18,000
We’re looking forward to it.

384
00:18:18,000 --> 00:18:21,000
We’ll decide on your fee
once we see what you can do.

385
00:18:21,000 --> 00:18:22,000
[excited chuckle]

386
00:18:23,000 --> 00:18:25,000
Great! Now that we’ve got that settled…

387
00:18:25,000 --> 00:18:27,000
-First things first…
-Huh?

388
00:18:27,000 --> 00:18:31,000
Can you teach me the doctoring methods
you talked about in the store earlier?

389
00:18:32,000 --> 00:18:33,000
-You really want to know?
-[Gon] Yep!

390
00:18:34,000 --> 00:18:37,000
Cauterizing and transplant and facelift.

391
00:18:37,000 --> 00:18:39,000
Is that it or are there others?

392
00:18:39,000 --> 00:18:40,000
You know something?

393
00:18:41,000 --> 00:18:42,000
None of that crap matters!

394
00:18:42,000 --> 00:18:45,000
[Gon] But they sound fun!
Kinda like magic tricks!

395
00:18:45,000 --> 00:18:47,000
[Killua] Yeah, well,
we’re not here to have fun!

396
00:18:49,000 --> 00:18:50,000
I think I get it now…

397
00:18:51,000 --> 00:18:53,000
why this kid intrigued me.

398
00:18:54,000 --> 00:18:58,000
He’s not concerned with
whether something is ‘good’ or ‘bad’.

399
00:18:58,000 --> 00:19:01,000
When I came clean
about making counterfeits,

400
00:19:02,000 --> 00:19:05,000
or when the men in the store
were talking about the vault…

401
00:19:06,000 --> 00:19:09,000
I didn’t see a hint of disapproval
or greed on his face.

402
00:19:09,000 --> 00:19:10,000
Not one.

403
00:19:12,000 --> 00:19:13,000
But what I did see...

404
00:19:14,000 --> 00:19:16,000
was pure curiosity!

405
00:19:17,000 --> 00:19:18,000
If something impresses him,

406
00:19:18,000 --> 00:19:21,000
he doesn’t start judging
whether it’s good or bad...

407
00:19:22,000 --> 00:19:25,000
which means he’s walking a fine line.

408
00:19:26,000 --> 00:19:28,000
He’s that rare kind of person

409
00:19:28,000 --> 00:19:31,000
who can never truly be appraised.

410
00:19:35,000 --> 00:19:36,000
Cauterization:

411
00:19:36,000 --> 00:19:39,000
Definitely the hardest
doctoring method to detect.

412
00:19:40,000 --> 00:19:42,000
But not too long ago

413
00:19:43,000 --> 00:19:44,000
a new method surfaced.

414
00:19:44,000 --> 00:19:46,000
It’s called an “autopsy”.

415
00:19:48,000 --> 00:19:51,000
That’s when you plainly
reveal the opened statue

416
00:19:51,000 --> 00:19:53,000
along with a fake treasure.

417
00:19:54,000 --> 00:19:55,000
It’s based on most people’s assumption

418
00:19:56,000 --> 00:19:59,000
that you wouldn’t open the statue
if the treasure were fake

419
00:19:59,000 --> 00:20:01,000
and that makes them easy to fool.

420
00:20:02,000 --> 00:20:05,000
But this method
is starting to get old now.

421
00:20:05,000 --> 00:20:07,000
People were getting suspicious,

422
00:20:07,000 --> 00:20:09,000
so of course
a new doctoring method emerged.

423
00:20:10,000 --> 00:20:12,000
Think you can guess? Give it a try.

424
00:20:13,000 --> 00:20:14,000
Oh, I know!

425
00:20:14,000 --> 00:20:15,000
The statue’s fake

426
00:20:15,000 --> 00:20:17,000
and the treasure inside of it
it’s fake, too!

427
00:20:17,000 --> 00:20:18,000
[Zepile] Wrong!

428
00:20:18,000 --> 00:20:19,000
-Oh...
-Wait. I got it!

429
00:20:19,000 --> 00:20:22,000
You take the treasure out
from a different opening!

430
00:20:22,000 --> 00:20:23,000
Bingo!

431
00:20:25,000 --> 00:20:28,000
You start by creating a new opening
and removing the treasure.

432
00:20:29,000 --> 00:20:33,000
Then, you just insert the fake treasure
and carefully seal the hole back up again.

433
00:20:34,000 --> 00:20:35,000
That’s known as an “ostomy”.

434
00:20:36,000 --> 00:20:37,000
An “ostomy”.

435
00:20:38,000 --> 00:20:41,000
Many veteran appraisers
have been deceived by it.

436
00:20:41,000 --> 00:20:44,000
If there are no signs
that the adhesive was discolored by fire,

437
00:20:45,000 --> 00:20:46,000
they assume that it’s real.

438
00:20:47,000 --> 00:20:50,000
And that, gentlemen,
is how you fool the pros.

439
00:20:51,000 --> 00:20:53,000
Ah! What an awesome world!

440
00:20:54,000 --> 00:20:55,000
[phone ringing]

441
00:20:56,000 --> 00:20:57,000
Uh, hello?

442
00:20:58,000 --> 00:20:59,000
A Spider?

443
00:21:00,000 --> 00:21:02,000
[Leorio] Yeah. It looks real.

444
00:21:02,000 --> 00:21:04,000
And there’s a video attached to it.

445
00:21:04,000 --> 00:21:06,000
We’ve got two targets.

446
00:21:06,000 --> 00:21:08,000
A man and a woman.

447
00:21:08,000 --> 00:21:10,000
I’ll head out right now,

448
00:21:10,000 --> 00:21:11,000
so meet me there.

449
00:21:11,000 --> 00:21:12,000
[Gon] Got it.

450
00:21:13,000 --> 00:21:15,000
-Come on. Let’s go!
-Okay.

451
00:21:16,000 --> 00:21:18,000
Hey! Wait a second!
What about the auction!

452
00:21:19,000 --> 00:21:20,000
You can handle it!

453
00:21:21,000 --> 00:21:22,000
Yeah, just try to get us a good price!

454
00:21:23,000 --> 00:21:24,000
Huh?!

455
00:21:27,000 --> 00:21:30,000
All right! You can count on me!

456
00:21:35,000 --> 00:21:38,000
[narrator] Gon and Killua
have had their eyes opened

457
00:21:38,000 --> 00:21:40,000
to a brand-new world.

458
00:21:41,000 --> 00:21:43,000
And they are about to make contact

459
00:21:43,000 --> 00:21:45,000
with the Phantom Troupe.

460
00:21:47,000 --> 00:21:50,000
[theme song playing]

461
00:22:56,000 --> 00:22:57,000
[Gon] Coming up:

462
00:22:57,000 --> 00:22:58,000
-Gon...
-[Killua] ...and Killua’s…

463
00:22:58,000 --> 00:23:00,000
[both] Hunterpedia!

464
00:23:00,000 --> 00:23:01,000
-I’m Gon!
-I’m Killua!

465
00:23:01,000 --> 00:23:03,000
[both] And this is our Hunterpedia!

466
00:23:03,000 --> 00:23:04,000
Today we’ll introduce Shizuku.

467
00:23:05,000 --> 00:23:07,000
Phantom Troupe member
with a vacuum cleaner named Blinky.

468
00:23:07,000 --> 00:23:09,000
But it can suck up the living!

469
00:23:09,000 --> 00:23:10,000
And its capacity is huge!

470
00:23:10,000 --> 00:23:12,000
Where do you go
if you get sucked up in it?

471
00:23:12,000 --> 00:23:13,000
Nobody knows!

472
00:23:17,000 --> 00:23:19,000
[Gon] Next time:
“Pursuit x and x Analysis.”

473
00:23:19,000 --> 00:23:21,000
-Right or left?
-[Killua] Right.

474
00:23:21,000 --> 00:23:24,000
-[Gon] Do we follow the man or the woman?
-[Killua] The woman.

475
00:23:24,000 --> 00:23:27,000
-[Gon] What’s better, red or blue?
-[Killua] You pick!
